#
# Record promoted runtime identities here after soak tests.
# Copy to models.lock on the development host. Do not invent digests.
#
# Intended Ollama pin: native macOS build (Homebrew or a GitHub release asset).
# After install, record `ollama --version` in ollama_version and `brew pin ollama`
# when using Homebrew. Do not pipe `curl https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh`
# without recording that version here. Leave Ollama/model digests empty until
# soak promotion. `deepseek_harness_version` is the B02 pin, not `latest`.

ollama_version: ""
upstream_model: qwen3.8:27b-mlx
upstream_digest: ""
alias: qwen38-agent-16k
alias_digest: ""
context_window: 16384
kv_cache: q8_0
flash_attention: true
sampling:
  thinking:
    temperature: 1.0
    top_p: 0.95
    top_k: 20
    min_p: 0.0
  non_thinking:
    temperature: 0.7
    top_p: 0.8
    top_k: 20
deepseek_harness_version: "dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.1"
notes: >-
  DSH pin is git tag dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.1 (commit
  cd5ef8148158c3a752a658978873241fdf8e2bbc), published 2026-08-27 as a
  developer-preview pre-release. Never use latest. The product is not
  security-audited; sandbox/approvals do not guarantee isolation. This cut
  enables public WebFetch by default — Majesta Two's profile overlay
  disables web fetch/search and session telemetry so cloud stays off until
  a later item sets cloud_allowed. ACP is complete in the pin; Majesta Two
  does not speak ACP yet (B09). Ollama compat: force system role
  (supportsDeveloperRole: false) and maxTokensField: max_tokens (ADR 0009).
  Ollama/model digests remain empty until B01 soak. See architecture §6.1
  and §18.
